      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, Congress enacted the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990 to prohibit the exclusion of people with disabilities from jobs, services, activities and other benefits. The Americans with Disabilities Act applies this prohibition of discrimination against people with disabilities to all activities of state and local governments. To ensure the City's compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, it is necessary to facilitate an effective means of cooperation, communication and coordination among the various agencies of the City.",
